<title>USA: Synthetic Industries Q2 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Synthetic Industries Q2 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>CHICKAMAUGA, Ga. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except share and per share amounts)</p>
<p>			Three Months Ended	 Six Months Ended</p>
<p>			  3/31/97     3/31/96    3/31/97    3/31/96</p>
<p> Net sales	   $ 75,356    $ 64,609   $146,211   $129,217</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>extraordinary item</p>
<p>			    2,158	 (410)	3,064    (2,307)</p>
<p>Extraordinary (loss)</p>
<p>			 (11,950)	   - -   (11,950)	  - -</p>
<p> Net loss	     (9,792)	 (410)    (8,886)    (2,307)</p>
<p>Income (loss) per share</p>
<p>before extraordinary item</p>
<p>			     0.24	(0.07)	 0.36     (0.39)</p>
<p>Extraordinary loss per share</p>
<p>			   (1.33)	   - -     (1.42)	  - -</p>
<p> Loss per share	(1.09)	(0.07)     (1.06)     (0.39)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>and common equivalent</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>			8,957,155   5,930,502  8,413,922  5,930,502</p>
<p>NOTE: The Synthetic Industries said its extraordinary loss for the second-quarter and six-month periods of 1997 resulted from the company's repurchase of its 12-3/4 percent senior subordinated debentures.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
